    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`) \u2014 there's a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event with minimal structural impact by keeping the entire change in one small, single-method class \u2014 `OwnerAuditListener` (`src/main/java/.../model/OwnerAuditListener.java`).\n\n**What changed in `onCreate`:**\n- Added a static `AtomicLong SEQ` for a monotonically increasing sequence across creates.\n- Extracted the membership-level computation to a local variable (removing the duplicated expression), reused by both the existing audit line and the new event.\n- Appended a second `AUDIT` line emitting the immutable JSON event `{\"seq\",\"ownerId\",\"customerCode\",\"membershipLevel\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\n**Why this shape:**\n- The cost formula multiplies by the number of files touched, so I deliberately avoided introducing a new `OwnerCreatedEvent` class/file (which would have roughly tripled the cost). Everything lives in the tiny existing listener, whose `WMC_other` is ~0.\n- `onCreate` stays cyclomatic-complexity 1 (straight-line code), and it's the only function touched, in the only file touched.\n- The event carries the owner's **current primary identifier** via `owner.getCustomerCode()`. When the customer code is later unified into the member id, that single accessor is the one point that changes, so the event will then carry the member id automatically.\n\nVerified output: `AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.",
